<%# KI-Pakete P4c (doc/ki_pakete_p4_plan.md E1): what a package switch already
    underway is doing, directly under the permanent "Aktuell" line — where the
    customer pressed the button and where they come back to look.

    STATIC on purpose, no polling frame. The build runs for minutes to hours, and a
    frame refreshing every few seconds would pay Embeddings::SwitchProgress's four
    anti-joins per interval per open tab — §5 Falle 1 amplified rather than avoided.
    A reload is honest and costs nothing.

    Reads @switch_progress (Embeddings::SwitchProgress::Result), assigned in
    AiSettingsController#load_package_catalogue. :none renders nothing. %>
<% if @switch_progress.present? && @switch_progress.state != :none %>
  <%# The visual states as DATA rather than as a four-branch cascade repeated for
      border, background, icon and text colour. Same reason as the controller's
      SEARCH_OUTCOMES (#437 review): a rule enforced by hand in four places drifts in
      one of them, and the drift is invisible in review.

      `.fetch` and NOT `.fetch(state, default)`: a state added to
      Embeddings::SwitchProgress::STATES without an entry here must fail loudly in the
      spec that pins the two together, rather than render in some arbitrary colour.
      That spec is spec/views/organisations/ai_settings/switch_progress_spec.rb — it
      renders EVERY state, so the missing key is a red example and never a customer's
      500 (P4c review, I3). %>
  <% tone = {
       building: { frame: 'border-cream-300 bg-cream-100', text: 'text-cream-900', icon: 'bi-arrow-repeat' },
       awaiting_flip: { frame: 'border-green-300 bg-green-50', text: 'text-green-900', icon: 'bi-check-circle' },
       paused: { frame: 'border-amber-300 bg-amber-50', text: 'text-amber-900', icon: 'bi-pause-circle' },
       retired_target: { frame: 'border-amber-300 bg-amber-50', text: 'text-amber-900', icon: 'bi-exclamation-triangle' }
     }.fetch(@switch_progress.state) %>

  <div class="mt-4 border rounded-lg p-4 <%= tone[:frame] %>"
       data-switch-progress="<%= @switch_progress.state %>">
    <p class="text-sm font-bold <%= tone[:text] %>">
      <i class="bi <%= tone[:icon] %> mr-1"></i>
      <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.progress.#{@switch_progress.state}_title") %>
    </p>

    <%# Only :building has numbers worth showing. :awaiting_flip measured a zero, and
        the other two would show a bar that cannot move — which is the very thing
        their own texts exist to explain. %>
    <% if @switch_progress.state == :building %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm tabular-nums <%= tone[:text] %>">
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.progress.building_body',
              remaining: number_with_delimiter(@switch_progress.remaining),
              total: number_with_delimiter(@switch_progress.total),
              percent: @switch_progress.percent) %>
      </p>
      <%# Decorative: the sentence above already carries the numbers, so a screen
          reader gets them once rather than twice. %>
      <div class="mt-2 h-2 rounded bg-cream-300 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="h-full bg-ink" style="width: <%= @switch_progress.percent %>%"></div>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm <%= tone[:text] %>">
        <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.progress.#{@switch_progress.state}_body") %>
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%# ONE search sentence, and it is true in every state that reaches this partial.
        Each of them has a resolved pointer — SwitchProgress returns :none without one
        — so the old space keeps serving until the flip and the Bestand stays findable
        throughout; only content created during the window is not, and that is said out
        loud.

        This used to be two sentences, the second one for orgs with no pointer, whose
        reads jump to the new empty space at once. That state no longer reaches this
        partial at all: it could not be detected without warning every healthy org too
        (P4c review, blocker 1), and it is reported to the OPERATOR instead, by
        `embeddings:check_alignment`. Do not reintroduce a reassuring/alarming split
        here without a detector that can tell the two populations apart. %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm <%= tone[:text] %>">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.progress.search_kept') %>
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>
